Third-party components included in lmdraw distributions

Project code
------------
The lmdraw source and the vendored cpp-dsl-sdk header are licensed under MIT;
see LICENSE.

LunaSVG 3.5.0 and PlutoVG 1.3.1
--------------------------------
The statically linked vector parser and rasterizer source is vendored in
third_party/lunasvg at upstream commit 83c58df8103dc7dca423dfd824992af94d49bed6.
LunaSVG and its bundled PlutoVG carry MIT licenses. PlutoVG includes raster
routines derived from the FreeType project under its FreeType Project License
(FTL), and the stb image and TrueType helpers carry public-domain notices.
Full MIT and FTL texts are in licenses/; the source files retain their original
stb notices.

Noto Sans
---------
Noto Sans Regular and Bold TrueType fonts are compiled into the executable and
are licensed under SIL Open Font License 1.1. The font copyright notice and
full license are in assets/fonts/OFL.txt and licenses/Noto-OFL-1.1.txt.

Linux C and C++ runtimes
------------------------
Linux release binaries statically include glibc, libstdc++, and libgcc runtime
objects. glibc is licensed under LGPL-2.1-or-later. GCC's libstdc++ and libgcc
are GPL-3.0-or-later with GCC Runtime Library Exception 3.1. Copies of the
relevant license texts are in licenses/. The project source, pinned rendering
source, build files, and font data are shipped as the corresponding source
bundle so users can rebuild and relink with a modified platform runtime.

Platform system libraries
-------------------------
macOS binaries link the operating-system libraries supplied by macOS. Windows
binaries use the MinGW-w64 toolchain with static compiler runtimes and import
only platform system libraries.
